1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,516
This is the last lecture of the class,

2
00:00:02,966 --> 00:00:04,844
and it doesn't teach you anything new.

3
00:00:05,744 --> 00:00:07,403
It asks you to finish.

4
00:00:09,203 --> 00:00:12,399
By the end you'll have played one whole evening

5
00:00:12,849 --> 00:00:15,585
in your own universe, with a list in your hand,

6
00:00:16,035 --> 00:00:19,128
and you'll know that every part of it works.

7
00:00:20,028 --> 00:00:22,527
You'll also know, honestly, what doesn't.

8
00:00:23,727 --> 00:00:24,982
Don't start the game yet.

9
00:00:25,882 --> 00:00:28,359
Write down where a crew will go, in order,

10
00:00:28,809 --> 00:00:30,816
and what should happen at each place.

11
00:00:32,617 --> 00:00:35,203
I've got six rows, in two sittings.

12
00:00:36,103 --> 00:00:39,322
The relay, the Tern, and the Assay Office.

13
00:00:40,222 --> 00:00:43,153
Then they save, and come back another night

14
00:00:43,603 --> 00:00:44,611
for the Bone Pile.

15
00:00:46,411 --> 00:00:47,852
I follow three rules.

16
00:00:48,752 --> 00:00:50,283
Three places make an evening.

17
00:00:51,183 --> 00:00:53,487
End a sitting somewhere safe,

18
00:00:53,937 --> 00:00:56,896
because the save keeps the system the crew is in.

19
00:00:57,796 --> 00:01:00,647
And put the save between the mystery and the fight,

20
00:01:01,097 --> 00:01:03,350
so they leave knowing where to go next.

21
00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:07,745
Now, ten lines of notes at the top of the main file.

22
00:01:08,645 --> 00:01:12,181
Two slashes start a note, so the game doesn't read these.

23
00:01:12,631 --> 00:01:13,667
They're there for people.

24
00:01:15,467 --> 00:01:19,412
Who the game is for, and the three dials from the battles lecture.

25
00:01:20,312 --> 00:01:21,997
The budget for my worst system,

26
00:01:22,447 --> 00:01:24,101
and then the two sittings.

27
00:01:25,901 --> 00:01:28,491
And the most useful part, the words.

28
00:01:29,391 --> 00:01:32,110
These are the words that have to match in two places,

29
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:35,374
and lint only checks the first of them for me.

30
00:01:36,274 --> 00:01:37,826
So when I rename something,

31
00:01:38,276 --> 00:01:40,263
this is my list of where else to go.

32
00:01:41,463 --> 00:01:43,347
There are four checks before I play.

33
00:01:44,247 --> 00:01:46,490
Lint says clean, for every file.

34
00:01:47,390 --> 00:01:48,815
The save is gone,

35
00:01:49,265 --> 00:01:51,748
because a run-through starts from a new game.

36
00:01:52,648 --> 00:01:54,833
The dials say what my card says.

37
00:01:55,733 --> 00:01:57,274
And the libraries are up to date.

38
00:01:58,474 --> 00:02:01,815
Here we go, and I tick each row as it happens.

39
00:02:03,615 --> 00:02:05,834
There are three leads in the Quest Log.

40
00:02:06,734 --> 00:02:10,135
On Comms, I hail the Compact and pay the levy.

41
00:02:11,035 --> 00:02:14,868
Now there's more work on offer, and the escort pays better,

42
00:02:15,318 --> 00:02:17,132
so I take it.

43
00:02:18,932 --> 00:02:20,010
On to the Tern.

44
00:02:20,910 --> 00:02:24,875
There's her card, and there's the warning from the battles lecture.

45
00:02:25,775 --> 00:02:29,065
The first lead is done, and a new step has appeared.

46
00:02:30,865 --> 00:02:32,316
Now the Assay Office.

47
00:02:33,216 --> 00:02:35,455
The escort pays out as I arrive.

48
00:02:36,355 --> 00:02:38,904
I ask about the Tern, and pay the fee.

49
00:02:39,354 --> 00:02:40,605
That closes the step,

50
00:02:41,055 --> 00:02:43,622
and it tells the crew where to go next.

51
00:02:45,422 --> 00:02:47,892
That's twelve rows, and twelve ticks.

52
00:02:49,092 --> 00:02:51,880
And now I close the game, on purpose.

53
00:02:52,780 --> 00:02:56,669
This is the part of an open universe that a single mission doesn't have.

54
00:02:57,569 --> 00:03:00,279
There's the save, and I'm going to leave it alone.

55
00:03:01,479 --> 00:03:03,037
I start it with the same line,

56
00:03:03,487 --> 00:03:06,498
and we're back at the Assay Office, with the same credits.

57
00:03:07,398 --> 00:03:09,534
The Quest Log is just as I left it.

58
00:03:11,334 --> 00:03:13,855
Now for the place the Gleaners won't talk about.

59
00:03:14,755 --> 00:03:15,998
Three cards come up.

60
00:03:16,448 --> 00:03:19,306
The place, the guards, and the one I wrote.

61
00:03:21,106 --> 00:03:22,337
Now I count the ships.

62
00:03:23,237 --> 00:03:24,649
Three are by the wreck,

63
00:03:25,099 --> 00:03:28,052
and four or five are right in front of me.

64
00:03:28,952 --> 00:03:30,845
That's the battle line from last time.

65
00:03:31,745 --> 00:03:34,252
If the dice made this an enemy system,

66
00:03:34,702 --> 00:03:37,037
there are more, a long way off.

67
00:03:38,837 --> 00:03:41,517
I have to tell you something about this last row.

68
00:03:42,417 --> 00:03:43,597
When I checked this page,

69
00:03:44,047 --> 00:03:46,614
a script told the game the four ships were destroyed.

70
00:03:47,514 --> 00:03:49,298
Nobody has fought this fight.

71
00:03:50,198 --> 00:03:53,092
So this is the first time, and we'll find out together.

72
00:03:54,292 --> 00:03:56,536
There are three things to read afterward.

73
00:03:57,436 --> 00:04:00,269
The runtime log, which should be empty.

74
00:04:01,169 --> 00:04:03,148
Your ticks, every one of them.

75
00:04:04,048 --> 00:04:06,856
And your standings, which should match the page.

76
00:04:08,656 --> 00:04:10,205
And then there's one more table,

77
00:04:10,655 --> 00:04:13,414
the things this universe doesn't do yet.

78
00:04:14,314 --> 00:04:16,966
An admiral's numbers can't be balanced yet.

79
00:04:17,866 --> 00:04:20,456
A captain can't be made a rival with one line.

80
00:04:22,256 --> 00:04:23,921
Neither of those is your mistake.

81
00:04:24,821 --> 00:04:26,365
But a writer who knows them

82
00:04:26,815 --> 00:04:29,437
writes around them, and that's why they're on the page.

83
00:04:30,637 --> 00:04:31,532
Now it's your turn,

84
00:04:31,982 --> 00:04:34,403
and this time it really is yours.

85
00:04:35,303 --> 00:04:37,751
Plan two sittings, and write your card.

86
00:04:38,651 --> 00:04:41,068
Write down what you should see before you play,

87
00:04:41,518 --> 00:04:42,737
from your own files.

88
00:04:44,537 --> 00:04:45,764
Then give it to a crew,

89
00:04:46,214 --> 00:04:48,287
sit behind them, and don't help.

90
00:04:50,087 --> 00:04:51,923
That's a whole universe, and you wrote it.

91
00:04:52,823 --> 00:04:54,385
Well done, and thank you.
